# polite phrases, after the Stanford politeness strategies (Danescu-Niculescu-Mizil et al. 2013):
# please, gratitude, apology, counterfactual modals ("could you", "would you"), deference, greetings.
# "can you" / "will you" are left out: they are how almost every command starts.
please
kindly
if you don't mind
if you do not mind
if you wouldn't mind
if you would not mind
would you mind
do you mind
if it's not too much trouble
if it isn't too much trouble
if you would be so good
if you would be so kind
would you be so kind
have the goodness
could you
could you possibly
would you
would you be able to
would it be possible
i was wondering if
i would appreciate
i'd appreciate
thank you
thanks
thank you very much
thanks a lot
many thanks
thanks so much
thank you so much
much appreciated
i appreciate it
cheers
sorry
sorry to bother you
excuse me
pardon me
my apologies
good morning
good afternoon
good evening
